## Production Environment (Windows Server 2025 + IIS)
- **Hosting**: IIS with HttpPlatformHandler → Node.js
- **`web.config`** sets `PORT=%HTTP_PLATFORM_PORT%` and `NODE_ENV=production`
- **`.env`** created by `deploy/install.ps1` on first install — contains `SESSION_SECRET` + `NODE_ENV=production`. Preserved on updates.
- **No reverse proxy or load balancer** in front of IIS
- **No auto-restart** mechanism beyond IIS app pool recycling
- **`AI_NAME_CODE` is NOT configured on the server** — AI name generator features are local-dev only
- **`CLAUDE_API_KEY`** status on server: unknown (may or may not be set)
- **Build process is local** (dev machine) → deploy built `dist/` to server

## Non-Negotiable Rules
1. NEVER call external APIs without user approval (state count + cost)
2. NEVER write to game_data_master.json without permission
3. Screenshots mandatory for classification
4. **OK% is the only accuracy metric** — adj% was removed (user decision). OK% = human-reviewed verdicts marked OK. Gate decisions use OK% thresholds (theme ≥87%, chars ≥85%, elements ≥60%, color ≥88%, overall ≥80%).
5. Run `--regression-full` after every pipeline change — report OK%, Res%, Wtd%, and health metrics
6. Scale slowly: verify at each batch before expanding
7. Every user verdict saved immediately to user_reviews.json
8. Screenshot quality validated by Claude (screenshot_quality field)
9. **Current accuracy** (429 scored, post-A10): theme 93.9% OK / 98.1% Res%, chars 91.1% / 97.9%, elements 64.3% / 96.3%, colors 95.6% / 98.1%, overall 86.2% / 97.6%. All gates PASSING.

